        "title": "feat(ui): add configurable chat send shortcut",
        "body": "Fixes #8147\n\nSupersedes #73390 with a maintainer-owned replay because the contributor branch is stale, conflicting, and does not allow maintainer edits.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where WebChat users who write multiline messages could not choose a modifier-based send shortcut, making accidental sends easy on desktop.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a gateway-scoped Chat setting for Enter or ⌘/Ctrl+Enter, using the existing Control UI settings owner instead of a standalone storage key. The composer keeps Shift+Enter and IME composition safe, exposes the active shortcut to assistive technology, and defaults to the existing Enter-to-send behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can choose their preferred send shortcut from Chat settings. The preference survives reloads for the same Gateway; plain Enter inserts a newline in modifier mode, while Ctrl+Enter and Command+Enter send.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwvcqmxsd2z4wnsxkt9vahzq`: `corepack pnpm ui:i18n:check` — 20 locales clean.\n- Same Testbox: `corepack pnpm test ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts` — 122 tests passed.\n- Same Testbox: focused mocked-Gateway Playwright E2E — persistence, default send, multiline draft, IME suppression, and modifier send passed.\n- Contract-driven visual run — four 1280×900 screenshots plus WebM inspected; transferred artifacts matched Testbox SHA-256 checksums.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nThe broad changed gate currently reaches an unrelated current-`main` typecheck failure introduced by #100788 (`SessionWorktreeInfo` and `SessionsCreateResult` unused exports); all preceding changed checks pass.\n",
